:4,"uses":376},{"base":"H0996","lemma":"בַּ֫יִן","tr":"ba·yin","gloss":"between","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":407},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":820},{"base":"H7971","lemma":"שָׁלַח","tr":"sha·lach","gloss":"to send: depart","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":847},{"base":"H1285","lemma":"בְּרִית","tr":"be·rit","gloss":"covenant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":284}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And when Abram heard that his relative had been captured, he mobilized the 318 trained men born in his household, and they set out in pursuit as far as Dan.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":20,"verse":9,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Abimelech called Abraham and asked, “What have you done to us? How have I sinned against you, that you have brought such tremendous guilt upon me and my kingdom? You have done things to me that should not be done.” Abimelech also asked Abraham, “What prompted you to do such a thing?”","from":3},{"book":"EXO","chapter":32,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“What did this people do to you,” Moses asked Aaron, “that you have led them into so great a sin?”","from":3},{"book":"JOS","chapter":9,"verse":19,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"All the leaders answered, “We have sworn an oath to them by the LORD, the God of Israel, and now we cannot touch them. This is how we will treat them: We will let them live, so that no wrath will fall on us because of the oath we swore to them.”","from":3},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Dilan, Mizpeh, Joktheel,","from":6},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":24,"verseEnd":26,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Chephar-ammoni, Ophni, and Geba—twelve cities, along with their villages. Gibeon, Ramah, Beeroth, Mizpeh, Chephirah, Mozah,","from":6},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Mizpeh, Chephirah, Mozah,","from":6},{"book":"JDG","chapter":2,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and you are not to make a covenant with the people of this land, but you shall tear down their altars.’ Yet you have not obeyed My voice. What is this you have done?","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"7-10":{"people":[{"id":"asa-h0609g","name":"Asa","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"hanani-h2607g","name":"Hanani","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"places":[{"id":"syria-h0758i","name":"Syria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"cush-h3568a","name":"Cush","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"libya-h3864","name":"Libya","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"words":[{"base":"H8172","lemma":"שָׁעַן","tr":"sha·an","gloss":"to lean","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":22},{"base":"H0609","lemma":"אָסָא","tr":"a·sa","gloss":"Asa","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":58},{"base":"H7203","lemma":"רֹאֶה","tr":"ro·eh","gloss":"seer","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1051},{"base":"H0758","lemma":"אֲרָם","tr":"a·ram","gloss":"Aram","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":143},{"base":"H2428","lemma":"חַ֫יִל","tr":"cha·yil","gloss":"strength: soldiers","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":246},{"base":"H6256","lemma":"עֵת","tr":"et","gloss":"time","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":296},{"base":"H3864","lemma":"לוּב","tr":"lu·vi","gloss":"Libyan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H4115","lemma":"מַהְפֶּ֫כֶת","tr":"mah·pe·khet","gloss":"stocks","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H2197","lemma":"זַ֫עַף","tr":"za·aph","gloss":"rage","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1PE","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":90,"source":"both","text":"For the eyes of the Lord are on the righteous, and His ears are inclined to their prayer. But the face of the Lord is against those who do evil.”","from":9},{"book":"PRO","chapter":15,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":63,"source":"both","text":"The eyes of the LORD are in every place, observing the evil and the good.","from":9},{"book":"JER","chapter":16,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":53,"source":"both","text":"For My eyes are on all their ways. They are not hidden from My face, and their guilt is not concealed from My eyes.","from":9},{"book":"PRO","chapter":5,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":46,"source":"both","text":"For a manʼs ways are before the eyes of the LORD, and the LORD examines all his paths.","from":9},{"book":"PSA","chapter":34,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":41,"source":"both","text":"The eyes of the LORD are on the righteous, and His ears are inclined to their cry.","from":9},{"book":"JOB","chapter":34,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":38,"source":"both","text":"For His eyes are on the ways of a man, and He sees his every step.","from":9},{"book":"HEB","chapter":4,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":33,"source":"both","text":"Nothing in all creation is hidden from Godʼs sight; everything is uncovered and exposed before the eyes of Him to whom we must give account.","from":9},{"book":"ZEC","chapter":4,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":32,"source":"both","text":"For who has despised the day of small things? But these seven eyes of the LORD, which scan the whole earth, will rejoice when they see the plumb line in the hand of Zerubbabel.”","from":9}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"11-14":{"people":[{"id":"asa-h0609g","name":"Asa","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0609","lemma":"אָסָא","tr":"a·sa","gloss":"Asa","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":58},{"base":"H2483","lemma":"חֳלִי","tr":"cho·li","gloss":"sickness","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":24},{"base":"H7901","lemma":"שָׁכַב","tr":"sha·khav","gloss":"to lie down: lay down","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":212},{"base":"H2177","lemma":"זַן","tr":"zan","gloss":"kind","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H4842","lemma":"מִרְקַ֫חַת","tr":"mir·qa·chat","gloss":"ointment","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H7543","lemma":"רָקַח","tr":"ra·qach","gloss":"to mix","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":877},{"base":"H8316","lemma":"שְׂרֵפָה","tr":"se·re·phah","gloss":"fire","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H3738","lemma":"כוּר","tr":"khur","gloss":"to dig","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H1314","lemma":"בֶּ֫שֶׂם","tr":"be·sem","gloss":"spice","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":29}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JER","chapter":17,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"This is what the LORD says: “Cursed is the man who trusts in mankind, who makes mere flesh his strength and turns his heart from the LORD.","from":12},{"book":"2CH","chapter":28,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"In the time of his distress, King Ahaz became even more unfaithful to the LORD.","from":12},{"book":"1CH","chapter":10,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"and he failed to inquire of the LORD. So the LORD put him to death and turned the kingdom over to David son of Jesse.","from":12},{"book":"2CH","chapter":16,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"For the eyes of the LORD roam to and fro over all the earth, to show Himself strong on behalf of those whose hearts are fully devoted to Him. You have acted foolishly in this matter. From now on, therefore, you will be at war.”","from":12},{"book":"MRK","chapter":5,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"She had borne much agony under the care of many physicians and had spent all she had, but to no avail. Instead, her condition had only grown worse.","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":50,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And Joseph directed the physicians in his service to embalm his father Israel. So they embalmed him,","from":14},{"book":"2CH","chapter":21,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"This continued day after day until two full years had passed. Finally, his intestines came out because of his disease, and he died in severe pain. And his people did not make a fire in his honor as they had done for his fathers.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":50,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Joseph directed the physicians in his service to embalm his father Israel. So they embalmed him,","from":12}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}